\begin{restatable}{theorem}{mlsitree}
        \label{thm:mlsi-bdd-growth-tree}
        Let $H$ be a $(\Delta,D)$-pseudorandom near-forest, and $J \in \R^{n \times n}$ an interaction matrix supported on $H$ with all interactions in $\left[ - \frac{\gamma}{\sqrt{D}} , \frac{\gamma}{\sqrt{D}} \right]$ for some $\gamma \in [0,1)$. There is a constant $c$ (depending on $\gamma$) such that for any external field $h \in \R^{n}$,
